      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Monitor the incision site for redness, swelling, or discharge daily, while ensuring her rumen motility has normalized via rectal palpation or ultrasound. Reject any feed offering until she shows consistent foregut vibrations with the intake of small amounts of wet alfalfa or beet pulp. If fever or lethargy develops, consult your veterinarian immediately, as delayed healing at this stage is critical.",
